<%# The charts, and the reasons there might not be any yet.

    Wrapped in a frame for a live run because which of these three it is
    CHANGES while the page is open: a run that is building its company has no
    series to draw, and a few seconds later it does. Deciding that once, when
    the page was rendered, meant the note stayed put and the charts only ever
    appeared on a refresh.

    The frame stops polling the moment there is something to draw, so the
    canvases are swapped in once rather than rebuilt every couple of seconds —
    which is what would make them flicker. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "run-charts" do %>
  <div data-controller="poll"
       data-poll-active-value="<%= seeding %>"
       data-poll-interval-value="2000"
       data-poll-url-value="<%= charts_run_path(stamp) %>">
    <% if seeding %>
      <p class="finding-body measure muted">
        The charts appear once the load test starts. Its company is being built
        first — see below.
      </p>
    <% elsif live || stored %>
      <%= render "shared/coping_charts",
            progress_url: progress_run_path(stamp, format: :json),
            live: live %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="finding-body measure muted">
        <strong>No delivery charts for this run.</strong> They are computed from k6's
        sub-second output on the machine that generated the load, and this run was
        imported before that payload was being saved. Run
        <code>bin/runner --rebuild-progress</code> there and publish again to fill
        them in.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
